            "review_title": "Review at La Bettola Saigon",
            "review_text": "Abocadosalada\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam13 contributions\n1\nReturned several times and will come back\nNov 2018 • Couples\nThis is my favorite Italian place to come with my bf besides Pasta Freska since it's close to our home (other nice place is Carpaccio but it's in the city center so we can't visit very often). My usual time to visit Bettola is during lunch time when it's not busy. Our favorite seat is the one indoor looking out the swimming pool, it's a nice view on a warm sunny day. Food takes time to come but the quality is 100% worth the wait. My favorite is always the homemade pasta with morel mushroom sauce, I LOVE mushroom and they are always generous with the portion and the sauce, which makes me happy every time. My bf on the other hand is a fan of their pizza, he even order delivery from them when I'm busy and he doesn't want to eat out alone. \n\nOnly two tiny points to improve that I would like to point out: one is the temperature of the tomato sauce paired with complementary bread basket. Sometimes they brought it out when it's still very cold, so even when I know it's not meant to be served hot, I think the sauce should be kept at somewhere closer to room temperature. The second point is background music, sometimes when we arrive they just blasted EDM pop songs at an unnecessary loud volume which doesn't set you on a right mood, so I think a little more gentle music would be great.\n\nThe service is great: attentive staff always be around with smile on their face so we would definitely come back.\n\nP/s: just checked other bad reviews stating about the out of stock and overcrowd issue, so I need to clarify that we always receive top food and service probably because we always come for lunch when it's usually super quiet. I think for better service residents in TD can try going there for lunch and I believe they won't be disappointed.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 30, 2018",
