            "review_text": "Vaughan1212\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam11 contributions\n1\nHome-made dough and fire oven makes the pizza special\nSep 2018 • Solo\nOne of best Diavola pizzas I've had, and the toppings are moist and generous without compensating by too much olive oil.\n\nRestaurant is aimed at locals and westerners with a Vietnamese buffet outside and a la carte menu in the AC section.\n\nPrice is about the same as I'd pay in the UK and reasonable for this quality of food. Good pizza chefs, stone fire ovens and fine ingredients don't come cheap.\n\nService was swift and accurate, didn't have to remind them of anything.\n\nWould definitely come again.\nRead more\nWritten September 20, 2018",
