            "review_title": "Review at La Bettola Saigon",
            "review_text": "Alexander H\nhochiminh city, Vietnam4 contributions\n0\nPizza Margherita bad surprise...\nDec 2017 • Family\nOur family (we are overseas Vietnamese) went there often, and the owner (he is from Italy) also knows us but we would like to share two no so good experience with you:\n1) Last time the restaurant was very full due to two groups of Japanese tourists, and often customers come to an Italian restaurant since they like having pizza. Rest owner said to us no more pizza, but after 5min we heard him talking in front of our table that there were two pizza left, and we ordered these last two (we believed). Then some Italian and European guests came, ordering pizza, but he did not say no more pizza, and with surprise there were enough pizzas for the western guests... We find this treatment not very fair and funny...\n2) Second experience was tonight, we came and the restaurant was very empty, we ordered as usual Pizza Margherita for starter, and several pasta dishes for main course. The pizza came out this time was not good, it was like an ice cream cake melting, we could not use fork or hand to pick it up and tasted terrible.. We made complaint to the Vietnamese waiter and asked him to tell the Italian chef, and he did. The waiter came back and apologize that the chef said he did wrong, put too much cheese on it and did not bake good enough.. we asked him to bring it back Later the Rest owner came out and complaint to us that we should have not do that, we asked why? He blamed that we should have told the chef not to put too much cheese etc. and I said \"sorry, this is the 10th time we come here and ordered the same pizza, we never said pls put more or less cheese, we just expected your rest should have delivered to us the same good pizza as usual but now you complaint to us and said this is our fault... I did not accept his accusation, but the guy carried on talking without listening to customers.. If there were western customers complaining he might treat them differently and accepted what he and his chef did wrong and did not charge the customers but it was not the case to us... \nAnd I would say this is the last time we came and for a very long while we are not coming to this restaurant anymore since we find 1) Treatment by the restaurant owner is not fair or bit with skin color 2) He blamed to customer instead coming to us saying apology this is very dumb and not polite from a restaurant owner... \nTherefore, I would not recommend anyone to come here unless you really want to taste the similar treatment and accusation...\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 13, 2017\ngiuseppe a\nDear Alexander, you must have a real big problem, you are just a liar and you are the racist in this case, since you are accusing me to be. Here in this restaurant we treat the customers all in the same way, no matter if different religion or color, people that think like you should stay away from pubblic environment especially restaurant.\nDo not dare to call me again like that, i hate racist people!\nWe are a respectable restaurant, we have customers and friends from all over the world, and \"scrocconi\" like you can be from eveywhere.\nSo is not about color but behavior, you can't eat more than half pizza and then complain for too much mozzarella and ask for one free pizza with less mozzarella.... This is why i came to your table and explain to you that if you want to complain for having a new pizza with less cheese you should do it before eating almost all of it.\nIf there is something wrong with your meal, you know from the first bite, you don't wait till the end,so you are even a liar, you just didn't accept the fact in front of your family that i was right and you were wrong, see customers not always are right.\nRegarding to your last visit, i'm going to explain again to you...\nLast time we had finish the pizza dough so no more pizza, then came up that we still have two dough, so i came to your table and say that if you still want we can make two more pizza,at the same time we were making a new fast dough just to finish the night,so the customers that came later they had to wait half hour for their pizza,at the end everybody were happy with their pizza, see an other lie from you....but i believe that everywere you go you think that people are just looking at your skin and bla bla bla....what a shame.\nAnyway, have a nice Christmas and New Year to you and your family.\nGiuseppe\nChef\nRead more\nWritten December 15, 2017\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
